MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_001: Hm, is this the right amount? Maybe I should crush\nit into smaller pieces...
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_002: Mu, what are you doing there? We sense that you\nare quite engrossed.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_003: I'm grinding some tree nuts. As for the tool,\nit's something I made myself.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_004: I thought it would be interesting to make a drink out\nof nuts and compare the flavor to coffee.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_005: Ah, so those nuts are a substitute for coffee...\nAnother insight into the Dagdan way of life!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_006: Oh, no. This isn't something Dagdans do—it's just an\nidea I had.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_007: I wanted to see, if I made a drink out of something\nother than coffee beans, how it'd turn out.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_008: But coffee is one of the pillars of this land's produce,\nis it not? Why seek an alternative to that bean?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_009: Are you plotting to overturn a cultural tradition of\nthe land and people that raised you?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_010: No, no, nothing so dramatic! I thought it would be\nfun to create something new.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_011: You know, make people happier? Even if only a\nlittle bit.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_012: There are lots of people who don't like how bitter\ncoffee is. This could be good for them!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_013: Then pursue your quest with vim and vigor! This\nmission seems worthy!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_014: And we will assist!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_015: Huh? I mean, you don't have to do that.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_016: There is no need for politeness. It is our pleasure.\nNow put us to work!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_017: Alright...sure. Can you help me grind down\nthese nuts, then?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_018: Hm... So we crush the nuts... Crush and crush...\nVery similar to making coffee.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_019: Be careful though—you don't want to use too\nmuch force.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_020: Worry not. We can manage such a task. This is\nsimplicity itself. Now— Hyah!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_021: Oh. That was a strange noise.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_022: Ahh! You broke my tool! What did I tell you?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_023: The device was no match for our vim. Bring us\nanother one, Mu!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_C_024: Ugh! Forget it. Keep your mouth shut and watch!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_001: Mu! We ourselves have found you a new nut!\nYou are very welcome to thank us.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_002: Oh, OK. Uh...thanks.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_003: But I'm in the middle of something. So step back.\nAnd don't touch anything this time!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_004: Yes, carry on! The great work must continue...\nwith these nuts!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_005: He really doesn't take a hint, does he...
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_006: Well, since you went to the trouble, I might as well\ntry 'em out. Here goes nothing...
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_007: We see you're using water of a tepid disposition. \nWould not boiling water be better?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_008: If we boiled it too much, it would lose its flavor!\nThis is the right temperature, trust me.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_009: But now—let's see! A pinch of these herbs could\nbring up the flavor...
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_010: Intriguing! Tell us more of Dagda's herbs! Should\nthey not all join this flavor festival?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_011: Would you stop butting in? I'm the one in\ncharge here.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_012: What next? Hmm, does the concoction want yet\nanother kind of new nut, perhaps?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_013: You're a strange guy, Peppe, being with me the\nwhole time I was working.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_014: I told you you could take a break, but here you are.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_015: Our duties as a king are ceaseless—among them,\nto learn everything about the land of Dagda.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_016: But we, at heart, enjoy new experiences.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_017: What is life in a city like? What moves its people's\nhearts? What novelties win their interest?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_018: We have long dreamed of experiencing it all!
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_019: And you, Mu...you brighten our days. Thank you.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_020: Hm. I guess, if you and me got sucked into some\nresearch together, it might be fun... Kinda.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_021: Peppe, what do you say you and me start\nworking together?
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_022: I'll keep a close eye to make sure my tools\ndon't break.
MID_SE_Moo_Pep_B_023: Aha! We are thrilled to hear it! Then, let this\nbeverage quest continue. Onward to glory!